The '''Living Cave''' is a sub-location of the [[Rift Dimension]]. It can be entered from the {{Zone|Village Plaza}}, through the {{Zone|Deja Vu Alley}}. 

The player can see into the '''Living Cave''' through the {{Zone|Dreadfarm}}, but the entrance is blocked off on both ends with {{Item|Barrier|link=}}s, requiring '{{Blue|[[wikt:intangibility|intangibility]]}}' to enter - or walking around, telegraphing that the '''Living Cave''' is inaccessible from the {{Zone|Dreadfarm}}.

{{RiftGuide|Craft Self-Recursive Pickaxe|Craft the Crux Heirloom|Enigma: Behind a Living Wall|Enigma: Flowery Message|Montezuma's Eight|souls=2}}

== Features ==
The '''Living Cave''' features many attractions. The player must have secured the {{Item|SkyBlock Citizen Timecharm}} and have a minimum of {{stat|rt|5:00}} remaining in order to access the location.

=== Living Metal Snakes ===
Living Metal Snakes move around the '''Living Cave'''. They appear as chains of {{Item|Blue Stained Glass|link=}} with a {{Item|Block of Lapis Lazuli|link=}} at the end, indicating its head. Snakes can be stopped with by pointing a [[Frozen Water Pungi]] at them, and can be mined from their tail blocks. They drop [[Living Metal Heart]]s once their heads are broken.

=== Living Stillness ===
{{Main|Living Stillness}}
The player can access the {{Zone|Living Stillness}} by going through the hole in the '''Living Cave'''. The player will receive Frostbite and begin losing {{Stat|rt}} if their Armor does not have Living Metal applied to it, obtained from [[Living Metal Capspawn]], [[Living Metal Chestspawn]], [[Living Metal Pantspawn]], and [[Living Metal Bootspawn]].

=== Enigma Souls ===
The '''Living Cave''' features {{Green|2}} [[Enigma Souls]].
